    "id": "train-3718",
    "question": "Tom opens an amusement park.  It cost $100,000 to open initially.  It also cost 1% of that to run per day.  He sells 150  tickets a day for $10 each.  How long will it take to make back his money?",
    "gold": "200",
    "answer": "It cost 100,000*.01=$<<100000*.01=1000>>1,000 a day to keep the place open\nHe makes 150*10=$<<150*10=1500>>1500 a day from the park\nSo he makes a profit of 1500-1000=$<<1500-1000=500>>500 a day\nSo it takes 100000/500=<<100000/500=200>>200 days to make back his money\n#### 200"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how long it will take Tom to make back his initial investment, we need to calculate his daily profit and then determine how many days it will take to cover the initial cost of $100,000.\n\n1. **Calculate the daily cost to run the amusement park:**\n   The daily cost is 1% of the initial cost.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Daily cost} = 0.01 \\times 100,000 = 1,000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the daily revenue from ticket sales:**\n   Tom sells 150 tickets a day at $10 each.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Daily revenue} = 150 \\times 10 = 1,500\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the daily profit:**\n   The daily profit is the daily revenue minus the daily cost.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Daily profit} = 1,500 - 1,000 = 500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the number of days required to make back the initial investment:**\n   The number of days required to make back the initial investment is the initial cost divided by the daily profit.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of days} = \\frac{100,000}{500} = 200\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, it will take Tom \\(\\boxed{200}\\) days to make back his money.",
